   395	### 7. The worker session, the argument vector, and the environment
   396	
   397	**DECIDED — session shape.** A `kotlin-native-v1` or
   398	`kotlin-native-repository-v1` operation uses **zero** graph-phase commands and
   399	exactly one compile-phase command. Decision 0008 section 7's "at most one" graph
   400	phase is what admits this, and Kotlin is the case it was written for: there is
   401	no dependency resolution to perform, because section 6 admits no package-supplied
   402	library and section 4 admits no dependency declaration, so the source set is
   403	decided by a manager-side directory walk rather than by asking a tool.
   404	
   405	**DECIDED — argument vector shape.** One process, one command, no retry, no
   406	daemon, no second phase:
   407	
   408	```text
   409	<jdk_root>/bin/java
   410	  -Dfile.encoding=UTF-8 -Duser.language=en -Duser.country=US
   411	  -cp <kotlin_root>/<compiler-jar-relpath>        [K-1]
   412	  <compiler-main-class>                            [K-1]
   413	  -produce program
   414	  -target <resolved native target>                 [K-6]
   415	  -o <operation-private-staging>/<command>
   416	  <absolute path to source 1>
   417	  …
   418	  <absolute path to source N>
   419	```
   420	
   421	with these binding rules:
   422	
   423	- sources are the recursive `.kt` set under `source_dir`, enumerated by the
   424	  manager, sorted by Unicode-scalar order of relative path, and passed as
