   150	
   151	**MEASURED — the direct form closes all of it.** Same shim `PATH`, invoking the
   152	JDK's `bin/java` directly with `-cp` into the Kotlin distribution:
   153	
   154	| Run | `PATH` resolutions | Exit | Artifact |
   155	|---|---|---|---|
   156	| control: `<kotlin_root>/bin/kotlinc …` | 4 (plus shebang `bash`) | 127 | none |
   157	| pinned: `<jdk_root>/bin/java -cp <kotlin_root>/… <MainClass> …` | **0** | 0 | produced |
   158	
   159	`<jdk_root>/bin/java` is a `Mach-O 64-bit executable arm64`.
   160	
   161	**Normative.** The driver MUST NOT execute `bin/kotlinc-native`, `bin/konanc`,
   162	`bin/kotlinc`, `bin/run_konan`, or any other launcher script from either
   163	distribution, on any platform, including for the version probe.
   164	
   165	**Process graph** bound to `manager-worker-v2`'s two lower nodes:
   166	
   167	```text
   168	manager parent
   169	  -> identity-verified manager-owned worker
   170	       -> <jdk_root>/bin/java
   171	            -> Kotlin/Native compiler, in-process, loaded by -cp from <kotlin_root>
   172	                 -> regular executables inside <kotlin_root>
   173	                    (code generator, assembler, archiver, linker)   [K-2]
   174	```
   175	
   176	**[K-1] Launcher shape.** Exactly two shapes are admissible and no third:
   177	
   178	- **(a) JVM-hosted.** The compiler is a JVM main class reachable by `-cp`. The
   179	  trusted launcher is `<jdk_root>/bin/java`; the `jdk` companion is REQUIRED.
   180	  Qualification records the exact jar relpath and main class.
   181	- **(b) Self-contained.** The distribution ships a regular, non-wrapper
   182	  executable that resolves nothing outside its own tree. That executable becomes
   183	  `primary_relpath` and the `jdk` companion list is empty.
   184	
   185	Under shape (a) the `kotlin` root contributes no launcher process and the
   186	pipeline's primary executable lives in the companion root. Decision 0010 section
   187	5 records why this is a completion of the reserved entry within decision 0007
   188	section 1.3's mandate rather than a widening of its section 3: every executed
   189	binary is still a regular file at a fixed relpath inside a fingerprinted,
   190	operator-trusted root; nothing is package-selected; no wrapper runs; no
   191	auto-install is introduced.
   192	
   193	**[K-2]** Every spawned child must resolve inside `<kotlin_root>` or
   194	`<jdk_root>`. Any other executable fails that platform. There is no toolchain
   195	identifier for a platform SDK that contributes a process, so Rust's data-only
   196	SDK root is not available as a precedent here.
   197	
   198	## 4. Source layout and the module file
   199	
   200	### 4.1 Local mode
   201	
   202	`build_roots` is the schema-6/7 model, unchanged: a portable relative path other
   203	than `.`, a real link-free directory in the immutable raw snapshot, unique and
   204	pairwise disjoint, never equal to or nested with a runtime root, referenced by
   205	at least one build command, statically excluded from agent context and from the
   206	runtime copy before cache lookup, identically for real builds, exact cache hits,
   207	and dry-runs.
   208	
   209	The build root MUST contain `kotlin-native-module.json` **directly**, and that
   210	file MUST be the nearest ancestor of `source_dir`. The manager does not search
   211	for it, does not walk upward, and does not infer it.
   212	
   213	### 4.2 External mode
   214	
   215	`skill-build.json` schema 2, target `driver: "kotlin-native-repository-v1"`,
   216	with `build_root`, `source_dir`, and the OPTIONAL `toolchain`. The command and
   217	descriptor drivers MUST be equal. The whole repository snapshot is the
   218	validation, identity, and audit subject; only the selected build root is
   219	compiler-visible; no external repository byte is agent-facing or runtime-copied.
   220	`kotlin-native-module.json` MUST exist directly in the descriptor's
   221	`build_root`. Against a schema-1 descriptor the command fails
   222	`build_descriptor_driver_unsupported`, with no fallback.
   223	
   224	### 4.3 `kotlin-native-module.json`
   225	
   226	```json
   227	{"schema_version": 1, "kotlin_version": "2.4.0"}
   228	```
   229	
   230	Exactly two members, both REQUIRED, `additionalProperties: false`.
   231	
   232	| Member | Type | Meaning |
   233	|---|---|---|
   234	| `schema_version` | `const` integer `1` | file-shape gate only |
   235	| `kotlin_version` | canonical `major.minor.patch` | the Kotlin compiler version the sources are written against |
   236	
   237	`kotlin_version` matches decision 0007 section 2.1's grammar exactly:
   238	`^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$`, each component at most
   239	`999999`, no prefix, no prerelease, no build metadata, no leading zeros, no
   240	wildcard.
   241	
   242	The file is never passed to the compiler, contributes no argument, and selects
   243	nothing.
   244	
   245	### 4.4 `source_dir` to program
   246	
   247	The program is the recursive `.kt` set under `source_dir`, compiled in `program`
   248	mode with the compiler's **default** entry point. The manager never names,
   249	searches for, or infers an entry point. Zero or multiple entry points is a
   250	compiler error and is therefore deterministic. No new command member is
   251	introduced, and the consuming manifest command key remains the sole naming
   252	authority for the artifact.
   253	
   254	## 5. Operation-private environment
   255	
   256	On top of the `manager-worker-v2` portable control set and the mandatory
   257	portable controls of `protocol/core.md` section 4.2.1:
   258	
   259	| Variable | Action | Reason |
   260	|---|---|---|
   261	| `JDK_JAVA_OPTIONS` | unset | **MEASURED**: honoured by the JVM launcher; injected `-Dprobe.marker=…` and `-XshowSettings:properties` and both took effect |
   262	| `JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS` | unset | **MEASURED**: honoured, `Picked up JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS: …` on stderr |
   263	| `_JAVA_OPTIONS` | unset | same family |
   264	| `CLASSPATH` | unset | would extend the compiler classpath |
   265	| `JAVA_HOME`, `JAVACMD`, `JAVA_OPTS` | unset | launcher-script inputs; closed structurally by section 3, unset as defence in depth |
   266	| `KOTLIN_HOME`, `KOTLIN_COMPILER`, `KOTLIN_TOOL`, `KOTLIN_RUNNER` | unset | same; `KOTLIN_COMPILER` selects the compiler main class |
   267	| `KONAN_DATA_DIR` | **set** to an operation-private empty directory | no read from or write to `~/.konan`; makes **[K-3]** decidable |
   268	| `PATH` | manager-owned minimal value | no toolchain is resolved through it |
   269	| `LANG`, `LC_ALL` | `C`/`POSIX` per the portable policy | locale-independent diagnostics |
   270	
   271	Both injection notices go to **stderr** while `java --version` stdout stayed
   272	byte-stable, which is why section 1.2's probe reads stdout.
   273	
   274	No manager-written configuration file is placed anywhere for this driver. Rust
   275	needed one because Cargo discovers ancestor `.cargo/config.toml`; the Kotlin
   276	pipeline reads no configuration file, because the launcher that would is never
   277	run and the compiler is given an explicit, complete argument vector.
   278	
   279	## 6. The worker session and the argument vector
   280	
   281	**Session.** Zero graph-phase commands, exactly one compile-phase command.
   282	Decision 0008 section 7's "at most one" graph phase admits this. No retry, no
   283	second phase, no daemon, no additional executable, no shell, no VCS operation,
   284	no dependency download, no generator, no test, no run, no tool request.
   285	
   286	The Kotlin compile daemon is **forbidden**: `kotlin-daemon.jar` and
   287	`kotlin-daemon-client.jar` ship in the distribution, and a daemon is a
   288	persistent process outside the session shape. The driver passes no daemon
   289	argument and MUST fail rather than fall back to one.
   290	
   291	**Compile vector.**
   292	
   293	```text
   294	<jdk_root>/bin/java                                            [K-1(a)]
   295	  -Dfile.encoding=UTF-8 -Duser.language=en -Duser.country=US
   296	  -cp <kotlin_root>/<compiler-jar-relpath>                     [K-1]
   297	  <compiler-main-class>                                        [K-1]
   298	  -produce program                                             [K-4 spelling]
   299	  -target <resolved default native target>                     [K-6]
   300	  -o <staging>/<command>                                       [K-4 suffix]
   301	  <abs source 1> … <abs source N>
   302	```
   303	
   304	Binding rules:
   305	
   306	1. **Sources are enumerated by the manager**, recursively under `source_dir`,
   307	   sorted by Unicode-scalar order of relative path, and passed as **absolute**
   308	   paths. A directory is never passed as a source root: that hands file
   309	   discovery to the compiler and would compile files the section 7 walk
   310	   rejected. **MEASURED**: `kotlinc -d out srcroot` does accept a directory and
   311	   does compile everything under it, which is exactly the behaviour being
   312	   refused.
   313	2. **Absolute form is load-bearing**, not cosmetic — see section 7.1.
   314	3. No entry point, module name, opt-in marker, `-language-version`,
   315	   `-api-version`, optimisation, debug, cache, memory-model, bitcode, library,
   316	   or plugin argument is passed, and none is package-derivable.
   317	4. `-target` names the host's own default native target only. **Cross-compilation
   318	   is not admitted.** A package cannot request a target and the driver never
   319	   selects one, so the representable-but-unserved-target gate that Rust and
   320	   Swift both required does not arise.
   321	5. **[K-4]** The exact produced filename, including any `.kexe` or `.exe`
   322	   suffix the compiler appends to `-o`, is measured at qualification. Any rename
   323	   happens **inside operation-private staging only**, before hashing and
   324	   publication.
   325	
   326	## 7. Pre-compile rejection matrix
   327	
   328	Decision 0008 section 7 requires an exhaustive, deterministic, pre-compile
   329	rejection matrix. Kotlin's code-execution surfaces are an open set — a
   330	general-purpose script engine, a script dialect the compiler can execute,
   331	annotation processing, compiler plugins, C interop — so the matrix is a **closed
   332	allow-list**, computed by a manager-side walk of the validated snapshot that
   333	runs no compiler and reaches no network.
   334	
   335	### 7.1 The allow-list
   336	
   337	The build root and every directory below it admit exactly three kinds of entry:
   338	
   339	| # | Admitted | Pattern |
   340	|---|---|---|
   341	| A1 | directories | name matches `^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*$` |
   342	| A2 | Kotlin sources | name matches `^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*\.kt$`, regular file |
   343	| A3 | the module file | exactly `kotlin-native-module.json`, regular file, **directly** in the build root and nowhere else |
   344	
   345	Anything else is `build_package_code_execution_forbidden`. The walk is total: it
   346	classifies every entry it encounters, follows no symlink, and has no
   347	depth, count, or size exemption that would leave an entry unclassified.
   348	
   349	The leading-character class excludes every dotfile **and every name beginning
   350	with `@`**, and the `@` exclusion is the one that is not obvious.
   351	
   352	**MEASURED — a filename alone is an argv-injection channel.** The Kotlin CLI
   353	expands a bare `@`-prefixed argument as a response file:
   354	
   355	| Argument form | Expanded | Outcome |
   356	|---|---|---|
   357	| `@inject` containing `-script`, plus a `.kts` file | **yes** | package code **executed**; marker file written; exit **0** |
   358	| `<abs>/…/@inject` | no | `error: source entry is not a Kotlin file`, exit 1 |
   359	| `./@inject` | no | same error, exit 1 |
   360	| `@atfile` containing `-verbose` | **yes** | compiler ran verbose; exit 0 |
   361	| `@nonexistent` | n/a | `warning: argfile not found: …`, exit **0** |
   362	
   363	A package shipping a file named `@x` in a directory the driver enumerates
   364	therefore executes arbitrary Kotlin at build time, through the compiler alone,
   365	with no Gradle and with a zero exit code — and a *missing* response file is only
   366	a warning, so a partial mitigation fails silently.
   367	
   368	Two independent layers close it, and both are required:
   369	
   370	- **normative** — A1/A2/A3 reject the name before the compile phase, which is
   371	  what decision 0008 section 7 demands;
   372	- **structural backstop** — rule 2 of section 6 passes every package-derived
   373	  path in absolute form, measured above to defeat the expansion. It is a
   374	  backstop and not the rule, because an argv convention is one implementation
   375	  slip from execution.
   376	
   377	### 7.2 Surfaces subsumed, with per-surface diagnostics
   378	
   379	Each row is a diagnostic beneath `build_package_code_execution_forbidden`, not a
   380	separate check; the allow-list is what rejects them.
   381	
   382	| Surface | Example entries | Diagnostic |
   383	|---|---|---|
   384	| response-file name | `@anything` | `kotlin_response_file_name_forbidden` |
   385	| Kotlin script source | `*.kts`, `build.gradle.kts`, `settings.gradle.kts` | `kotlin_script_source_forbidden` |
   386	| build-system file | `build.gradle`, `settings.gradle`, `gradle.properties`, `gradlew`, `gradlew.bat`, `gradle/`, `.gradle/`, `pom.xml`, `.mvn/`, `mvnw` | `kotlin_build_system_file_forbidden` |
   387	| annotation processing / plugin config | kapt or KSP directories, `META-INF/services`, `*.pro` | `kotlin_build_system_file_forbidden` |
   388	| C interop input | `*.def`, `*.h`, `*.c`, `*.m`, `*.mm`, `*.cpp`, `*.s`, `*.S`, `*.o`, `*.a`, `*.so`, `*.dylib`, `*.dll`, `*.lib` | `kotlin_native_interop_input_forbidden` |
   389	| prebuilt library | `*.klib`, `*.jar`, `*.aar` | `kotlin_prebuilt_library_forbidden` |
   390	| any other file | anything not A2 or A3 | `kotlin_non_source_entry_forbidden` |
   391	| non-regular entry | symlink, device, socket, FIFO | `kotlin_non_regular_entry_forbidden` |
   392	
   393	`.kts` deserves its measured nuance rather than an overstatement. **MEASURED**:
   394	a `.kts` file reaching the compiler *without* `-script` was compiled into a
   395	class and **not** executed — the marker was absent, `Evil.class` was produced,
   396	exit 0. It is inert alone, and it is the payload half of the `@` vector. Its
   397	behaviour under the native backend is **[K-5]**; the allow-list rejects it
   398	either way.
   399	
   400	### 7.3 Surfaces closed structurally rather than by the walk
   401	
   402	These are argv-only and unreachable because the closed command surface gives a
   403	package no way to supply an argument and the driver's vector is fixed. They are
   404	listed so the matrix is exhaustive over *surfaces*, and so that any future change
   405	letting package data reach argv is visibly a change to this section.
   406	
   407	| Surface | Flag | Why unreachable |
   408	|---|---|---|
   409	| compiler plugin by classpath | `-Xplugin=<path>` | not in the vector; no package-controlled argv |
   410	| compiler plugin, new form | `-Xcompiler-plugin=<path>…`, `-Xcompiler-plugin-order=…` | same |
   411	| plugin option | `-P plugin:<id>:<opt>=<v>` | same |
   412	| script templates | `-script-templates`, `-Xdefault-script-extension`, `-Xscript-resolver-environment` | same |
   413	| explicit script execution | `-script`, `-expression`/`-e` | same, **and** reachable only through the `@` vector that 7.1 rejects |
   414	| JVM passthrough | `-J…`, `-D…` | launcher-script features; the launcher is never run |
   415	
   416	### 7.4 Network
   417	
   418	No dependency resolution exists to perform: section 4 admits no dependency
   419	declaration and section 7.1 admits no prebuilt library, so there is nothing to
   420	fetch. `KONAN_DATA_DIR` points at an operation-private empty directory, so a
   421	distribution that would materialise LLVM or a sysroot on first use cannot reach
   422	a shared cache and fails visibly. **[K-3]** is the qualification test that it
   423	does not need to.
   424	
   425	## 8. Stage B — metadata disposition
   426	
   427	Runs after local snapshot validation, or after exact external acquisition and
   428	audit, and before any artifact-cache candidate is read or any compiler child is
   429	started. Ordered steps per decision 0007 section 4: recompute the effective
   430	requirement now that the descriptor requirement is readable, re-evaluate the
   431	resolved version against the narrowed interval, gate on file shape, then
   432	evaluate dispositions.
   433	
   434	### 8.1 File-shape gate
   435	
   436	`build_toolchain_metadata_mismatch`, before cache lookup, if any of:
   437	
   438	1. `kotlin-native-module.json` is absent from the build root, is not a regular
   439	   file, or is present anywhere other than directly in the build root;
   440	2. it is not well-formed JSON, or is not a JSON object;
   441	3. `schema_version` is absent or is not the integer `1`;
   442	4. `kotlin_version` is absent;
   443	5. any member other than those two is present;
   444	6. a member is duplicated.
   445	
   446	### 8.2 Disposition table
   447	
   448	| File | Field | Disposition | Rule |
   449	|---|---|---|---|
   450	| `kotlin-native-module.json` | `kotlin_version` | `compared` | canonical triple; strictly above the resolved compiler triple ⇒ `build_toolchain_metadata_mismatch` |
   451	| `kotlin-native-module.json` | `schema_version` | file-shape gate only | not a metadata source |
   452	
   453	There is **no `forbidden` class**, because the field's value space is a version
   454	and nothing else — no spelling of it names *where* a toolchain comes from.
   455	
   456	### 8.3 The classifier is two classes
   457	
   458	| Class | Condition | Disposition |
   459	|---|---|---|
   460	| C1 | matches the canonical triple grammar exactly | `compared` |
   461	| C2 | anything else | `build_toolchain_metadata_mismatch` (8.1 step 4 or the grammar) |
   462	
   463	Total by construction, with C2 as the mandatory catch-all. Because Curator owns
   464	the grammar, there is no document layer, no ecosystem grammar layer, and no
   465	edition floor for the layers to be independent of. Decision 0007's alignment
   466	properties reduce accordingly: the security partition `F` is empty, so P1
   467	(`C ⊆ Upstream`) and P2 (`Upstream \ F ⊆ C`) collapse to the satisfiable
   468	equality `C = Upstream`, where `Upstream` is Curator's own canonical grammar.
   469	Both hold trivially and are checked as such.
   470	
   471	## 9. Identity, cache, receipt, marker, claim
   472	
   473	`curator-build-source-v1` is reused unchanged for both source modes. The
   474	protected external snapshot key of `protocol/core.md` section 9.4 is unchanged.
   475	
   476	The logical cache key is the SHA-256 of `CCJ-1` over the complete build input,
   477	which binds:
   478	
   479	| Input | Local | External |
   480	|---|---|---|
   481	| `receipt_schema_version` | `3` | `4` |
   482	| `driver` | `const kotlin-native-v1` | `const kotlin-native-repository-v1` |
   483	| source state | `curator-build-source-v1` over the raw snapshot | repository snapshot identity per decision 0005 |
   484	| consuming command name | yes | yes |
   485	| build root and `source_dir` | yes | yes |
   486	| native target | resolved default target **[K-6]** | same |
   487	| `toolchain_identities` | ordered `[kotlin, jdk]` (or `[kotlin]` under shape (b)) | same |
   488	| policy object | closed, below | same |
   489	
   490	Policy object, closed to exactly two members:
   491	
   492	```json
   493	{"execution_policy": "manager-worker-v2", "compile_profile": "kotlin-native-program-v1"}
   494	```
   495	
   496	`execution_policy` is the `const` decision 0008 section 2's closed table binds to
   497	these identifiers. `compile_profile` is a `const` naming the session shape, the
   498	source-enumeration rule, and the default-entry-point mapping together, so that a
   499	future semantic change to any of them cannot happen without a cache-identity
   500	change — decision 0006's reason for binding the process graph into the input,
   501	applied to the one place Kotlin's semantics could otherwise move silently.
   502	
   503	The effective toolchain requirement and the `compatibility` set are gates, not
   504	build inputs, so the wire `toolchain` object never enters a cache key, receipt,
   505	marker, or claim. What enters is the resolved identity.
   506	
   507	Install marker v4 records `driver`, `receipt_schema_version`, and
   508	`execution_policy` per entry; a reader validates both recorded values against
   509	decision 0008 section 2's closed tables and rejects a mismatch rather than
   510	inferring. Top-level `build_source` is REQUIRED exactly when at least one active
   511	local build command of any admitted local driver exists.
   512	
   513	Claim schema 4 asserts these identifiers **only if** section 11 admitted at
   514	least one tuple. Otherwise decision 0010 section 10 applies and they are
   515	unassertable.
   516	
   517	## 10. Artifact
   518	
   519	`native-executable-v1`, and nothing else:
   520	
   521	- exactly one bounded regular file, produced into operation-private staging,
   522	  hashed there, published immutably under the manager-home mutation lock;
   523	- named solely by the manager from the consuming manifest command key, as
   524	  `bin/<command>` on Unix and `bin/<command>.exe` on Windows;
   525	- directly executable by the host program loader using only base-installation
   526	  libraries;
   527	- never executed by the manager during validation, installation, status, repair,
   528	  rollback, or garbage collection.
   529	
   530	By-products stay in staging and are discarded with it: `.klib` intermediates,
   531	the compiler cache, `*.dSYM`/`*.pdb` debug output, `.kexe.dSYM` bundles, and any
   532	`konan` temporary tree. None enters cache identity, the receipt, the marker, the
   533	shim relationship, or publication.
   534	
   535	Bit-reproducibility is not required. A linker-applied ad-hoc signature is
   536	compiler output, not a manager signing step, and must be produced by the fixed
   537	vector without selecting a signing identity, credential, or network interaction.
   538	
   539	### 10.1 Signing and credential boundary
   540	
   541	Unchanged from decision 0008 section 9, restated because macOS makes it
   542	concrete:
   543	
   544	- neither driver performs manager post-build signing, timestamping, or
   545	  notarization;
   546	- no manifest, descriptor, module file, or repository byte may select a signing
   547	  identity, certificate, entitlement, provisioning profile, keychain, or
   548	  notarization credential — no such field exists, and none may be added;
   549	- `codesign`, `productsign`, `notarytool`, `stapler`, and `signtool.exe` MUST
   550	  NOT appear anywhere in the process graph. On macOS their appearance also fails
   551	  Q3;
   552	- a platform policy that requires a locally signed binary MUST reject the build
   553	  until the separately versioned and reviewed signer profile of
   554	  `protocol/core.md` section 12.2 exists. It MUST NOT be answered by a
   555	  self-signed identity, an ad-hoc `codesign` invocation, or a
   556	  quarantine-attribute removal;
   557	- credentials, host-verification state, transport executables, proxy policy,
   558	  timeouts, and authentication modes stay operator-owned and MUST NOT appear in
   559	  a manifest, descriptor, repository, module file, compiler environment, receipt
   560	  trust field, or marker.
   561	
   562	## 11. Platform matrix and qualification
   563	
   564	`platforms` is **empty** for both identifiers. No tuple is claimed.
   565	
   566	A `(driver, operating_system, architecture)` tuple is admitted only when a run
   567	on that exact tuple, on an immutable native host, produces all of Q1–Q9 with
   568	recorded argv and real exit codes.
   569	
   570	### 11.1 The acceptance test
   571	
   572	| # | Requirement |
   573	|---|---|
   574	| Q1 | Distribution resolves from a trusted origin; **[K-1]** and **[K-7]** answered — launcher, entry point, probe vector, anchored normalization with its stream named and the native backend token asserted |
   575	| Q2 | Shim-`PATH` run of the full compile records **0** `PATH` resolutions, **and** the paired control through the shipped launcher records a non-zero count. Without the control firing the zero proves nothing |
   576	| Q3 | Every spawned child is a regular file inside `<kotlin_root>` or `<jdk_root>`, recorded by resolved absolute path — **[K-2]** |
   577	| Q4 | With `KONAN_DATA_DIR` at an operation-private empty directory and no reachable network, the compile succeeds and that directory is unchanged — **[K-3]** |
   578	| Q5 | Exactly one file produced for the build; exact name recorded — **[K-4]**; renamed inside staging only; no by-product published |
   579	| Q6 | Published file is a native executable for the tuple, runs, and every dynamic dependency is a base-installation library |
   580	| Q7 | Default native target read from the distribution's own output and mapped to `(operating_system, architecture)` — **[K-6]** |
   581	| Q8 | Section 7.1 exercised with at least one positive case and one rejected case per row of 7.2, including the `@`-name case and the `.kts` case |
   582	| Q9 | `compatibility` gains the tested family, and only that family, after the driver's conformance vectors pass against it |
   583	
   584	### 11.2 macOS
   585	
   586	The Apple linking path is decisive. If `clang`, `ld`, `libtool`, `xcrun`,
   587	`dsymutil`, `install_name_tool`, or `codesign` is spawned from outside a
   588	fingerprinted root, the tuple fails Q3 and macOS is **not admitted**. An
   589	implementation MUST NOT answer this by resolving a host tool, shipping a shim,
   590	or declaring an SDK data-only while executing from it. `macos/arm64` and
   591	`macos/amd64` are separate tuples and neither implies the other.
   592	
   593	### 11.3 Windows
   594	
   595	An implementation MUST NOT resolve `cmd.exe`, `powershell.exe`, `link.exe`,
   596	`cl.exe`, `lib.exe`, `vswhere.exe`, or a Visual Studio activation script. The
   597	MinGW-family linking path must be shown to live inside `<kotlin_root>`.
   598	`windows/amd64` and `windows/arm64` are separate tuples.
   599	`TASK-260729-rhjxtx` measured that no Kotlin toolchain of any backend exists on
   600	the reachable Windows host, so both remain unqualified.
   601	
   602	### 11.4 Linux
   603	
   604	Excluded until `TASK-260728-1skseh`, then qualified by `TASK-260728-3u1nho` with
   605	the identical Q1–Q9 test plus the base-installation dependency check of Q6.
   606	
   607	### 11.5 Retirement
   608	
   609	If no tuple has passed Q1–Q9 when `TASK-260728-251p01` mints manifest schema 8,
   610	both identifiers are retired unused: not reassigned to another language,
   611	backend, artifact class, or source mode, and not enabled by relaxing another
   612	driver. Claim schema 4 is then minted over six identifiers and both become
   613	structurally unassertable.
   614	
   615	## 12. Diagnostics
   616	
   617	| Code | Fires when |
   618	|---|---|
   619	| `build_package_code_execution_forbidden` | any section 7.1 allow-list rejection, with the section 7.2 per-surface diagnostic in the payload |
   620	| `build_toolchain_metadata_mismatch` | section 8.1 file-shape gate, or `kotlin_version` strictly above the resolved triple |
   621	| `build_toolchain_requirement_invalid` | `toolchain.id` not `kotlin`; malformed requirement literal |
   622	| `build_toolchain_requirement_unsatisfiable` | empty intersection of baseline, manifest, and descriptor requirements |
   623	| `build_toolchain_version_undetermined` | probe output unmatched or multiply matched by the anchored rule |
   624	| `build_toolchain_untested_release` | resolved family not in `compatibility` — which, while `compatibility` is empty, is **every** resolved version |
   625	| `platform_unsupported` | host `(os, arch)` not in `platforms` — which, while `platforms` is empty, is **every** host |
   626	| `build_artifact_class_unsupported` | a platform that cannot produce a single directly loadable file |
   627	| `build_descriptor_driver_unsupported` | schema-1 descriptor named by a `kotlin-native-repository-v1` command |
   628	| `build_descriptor_schema_unsupported` | unsupported descriptor version |
   629	| `build_execution_control_unavailable` | any mandatory portable control unavailable, unchanged under `manager-worker-v2` |
   630	
   631	The two rows marked "every" are the honest current state, not a defect: while
   632	both sets are empty, an implementation that resolves a Kotlin toolchain at all
   633	fails closed, which is the correct behaviour for a reserved identifier.
   634	
   635	## 13. Capability limitations
   636	
   637	Authoring guidance (`TASK-260728-2uh7em`) MUST carry all four:
   638	
   639	1. **No third-party dependencies.** No `.klib` may be supplied or named, and the
   640	   vector passes no `-library`. A build root compiles against the distribution's
   641	   standard library only.
   642	2. **No C interop.** `cinterop` is a second tool and a second command;
   643	   `manager-worker-v2` admits neither.
   644	3. **The build root is not an IDE project.** Section 7.1 excludes Gradle files.
   645	   An author keeps the IDE project outside the build root; build roots are
   646	   context-excluded and never runtime-copied, so this costs the agent nothing
   647	   and costs the author a duplicated source layout.
   648	4. **No cross-compilation.** One host builds for its own target only.
   649	
   650	## 14. Conformance vector inventory
   651	
   652	Vectors are authored by `TASK-260728-251p01` only if section 11.5 does not
   653	retire the identifiers. The inventory this reference fixes:
   654	
   655	| Group | Cases | Notes |
   656	|---|---|---|
   657	| reserved-identifier rejection | 10 | each frozen manifest, descriptor, receipt, marker, and claim schema rejects both identifiers |
   658	| command shape | 8 | `buildCommandV8` and `repositoryBuildCommandV2` with the `kotlin-native` consts; missing member; extra member; `toolchain.id` not `kotlin` |
   659	| descriptor | 4 | schema-2 positive; schema-1 with a Kotlin driver ⇒ `build_descriptor_driver_unsupported`; unknown schema; command/descriptor driver mismatch |
   660	| module file shape | 12 | six 8.1 gate cases, plus duplicate member, non-object, wrong `schema_version` type, absent file, file outside the build root, file not a regular file |
   661	| `kotlin_version` classifier | 10 | C1 equal, C1 below, C1 above ⇒ mismatch; C2 for prefix, prerelease, build metadata, leading zero, two-component, wildcard, empty |
   662	| allow-list | 22 | one positive and one rejected case per row of 7.2, plus the `@`-name case, the `.kts` case, a nested directory, a rejected directory name, a symlink, and the module file placed outside the root |
   663	| requirement intersection | 6 | baseline ∩ manifest ∩ descriptor, including the non-empty-but-excludes-resolved case decision 0007 section 4 names |
   664	| policy and identity | 6 | policy object closed to its two members; `execution_policy` const; `compile_profile` const; `toolchain_identities` ordering; v1/v2 non-aliasing; receipt schema 3 vs 4 |
   665	| platform | 4 | empty `platforms` ⇒ `platform_unsupported` on every host; empty `compatibility` ⇒ `build_toolchain_untested_release` on every resolved version |
   666	
   667	Every vector declares the `compatibility` set and the `platforms` set as fixture
   668	input, so outcomes are deterministic across managers, exactly as decision 0007
   669	section 1.1.1 requires.

